<title>UK: Granada sells Plaza Athenee for 45 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Granada sells Plaza Athenee for 45 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Granada Group Plc said on Monday it had sold the Plaza Athenee hotel in Paris to a group of Brunei-based investors for 45 million stg.</p>
<p>In a statement, the hotels and leisure group said the sale was made to PA Holdings (L) France S.A., a company controlled by investors in Brunei.  </p>
<p>Granada said the luxury hotel made pretax profits of 0.2 million stg on turnover of 20.9 million stg in the year ending January 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Net assets attributable to the property being sold were 35 million stg at January 31, 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
